SUMMARY:[現場] The Defiant Girl and the Incomplete Gentleman - Tobias War
 ner
LOCATION:Encina Commons\, Room 123
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-defiant-girl-and-the-incomplete-g
 entleman-tobias-warner
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54419015357018.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/the-
 defiant-girl-and-the-incomplete-gentleman-tobias-warner\n報名/票券: ht
 tps://forms.gle/hxm6UQsYrurBToVL6\n\nSession Description:\n\nThis talk wil
 l explore the circulation of one of the most widespread yet understudied n
 arratives in the world – a tale of desire\, deception\, and escape told 
 all over the African continent and spread across the globe by slavery and 
 imperialism. The story tells of a defiant young woman who refuses all suit
 ors only to fall in love with a handsome stranger. But when that stranger 
 turns out to be an evil creature in disguise who has assembled a human bod
 y for himself out of rented parts\, the young woman must find a way to esc
 ape. Probably the best-known version of this tale is the story of the ‘c
 omplete gentleman’ recounted by Amos Tutuola in The Palm-Wine Drinkard b
 ut over the last two centuries hundreds of versions of this narrative have
  been collected\, adapted\, and reimagined across the African continent an
 d the Atlantic and Indian Ocean worlds by creative writers\, artists\, and
  thinkers including Ama Ata Aidoo\, Lydia Cabrera\, Maryse Condé\, David 
 Diop\, Melville and Frances Herskovits\, Langston Hughes\, Ahmadou Kouroum
 a\, Alan Lomax\, Taban Lo Liyong\, Achille Mbembe\, Ngũgĩ Wa’Thiongo\,
  Okot p’Bitek\, and Efua Sutherland. This talk will investigate the form
 s of aesthetic\, scholarly\, and political imagination that have emerged a
 round this story. By bringing into view a narrative constellation that str
 etches across Africa and its diasporas\, this project aims to rethink the 
 study of literature at a global scale.\n\nSpeaker Biography:\n\nTobias War
 ner is Associate Profess
END:VEVENT
