DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54499291152003.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/2026
 -saroyan-prize\n報名/票券: https://forms.gle/rJfz4qazRpBpysFK9\n\nPlea
 se join us as we celebrate the winners of the 2026 William Saroyan Interna
 tional Prize for Writing!\n\nJustin Haynes\nfiction winner and author of\n
 Ibis\n&\nChloe Dalton\nnonfiction winner and author of\nRaising Hare\n(Chl
 oe will be presenting via recorded remarks)\n\nTuesday\, December 8\, 2026
 \n4:30 to 6:30 pm\nGreen Library\, 5th floor\, Bender Room\n\nThe event wi
 ll feature remarks and readings by Justin Haynes in person and Chloe Dalto
 n via pre-recorded video. Both authors’ books will be available for purc
 hase.\n\nPlease register if you would like to attend.\n\nJustin Haynes’ 
 debut novel\, Ibis (Abrams\, 2025)\, and Chloe Dalton’s memoir\, Raising
  Hare (Pantheon Books\, 2025) are the recipients of the 2026 William Saroy
 an International Prize for Writing administered by Stanford University Lib
 raries and the William Saroyan Foundation. The biennial prize honors the l
 ife and legacy of novelist\, playwright\, and short-story author William S
 aroyan by encouraging and recognizing new and emerging writers.\n\nLearn m
 ore about the winners and their books.
