BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54535252808070@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261117T153012Z
DTSTART:20261204T203000Z
DTEND:20261204T213000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] FIRST FRIDAY | Playbill: How a Theatre Program Became an I
 nstitution
LOCATION:Roble Gym\, R137
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/FF-DEC-2026
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54535252808070.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/FF-D
 EC-2026\n\nDEC FIRST FRIDAY | MEMAUD 125 | Open to the Stanford Community 
 | Lunch will be served.\n\nThe TAPS Graduate Students host Dr. Vicki L. Ho
 skins for the December First Friday.\n\nHave you ever given much thought t
 o your theatrical program after the usher hands it to you? This talk asks 
 you to consider what role a theatrical program plays in shaping Broadway
 ’s cultural identity. Together\, we will explore the central argument of
  Playbill’s Broadway: Monopolies\, Branding\, and Audience Life\, examin
 ing how Playbill evolved from a commercial printing and advertising enterp
 rise into an influential cultural institution. Along the way\, we’ll ref
 lect on our own relationships with playbills\, considering how their famil
 iar presence in the theatre-going experience shapes our theatrical expecta
 tions. You'll never see a theatrical program the same way.\n\nABOUT THE SP
 EAKER | Dr. Vicki L. Hoskins is an Assistant Professor of Theatre and Danc
 e at San Francisco State University. Her research investigates the economi
 c and cultural structures that shape the production\, circulation\, and re
 ception of theatre\, with particular attention to Broadway\, musical theat
 re\, branding\, marketing\, and audience culture. Her current book project
 \, Playbill’s Broadway: Monopolies\, Branding\, and Audience Life\, trac
 es the institutional history of Playbill and examines how the company’s 
 commercial strategies\, industry relationships\, and branding practices ha
 ve shaped Broadway’s cultural identity and audience experiences. Her
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54540964348970@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261117T155440Z
DTSTART:20261202T200000Z
DTEND:20261202T200000Z
SUMMARY:[線上] CREATE Webinar - Enhancing Parent-Led Interventions Throug
 h Artificial Intelligence
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/parent-led-interventions
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54540964348970.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/pare
 nt-led-interventions\n報名/票券: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/regi
 ster/WN_rhfhY3knQ8Kb9XOEx5ApCw\n\nJoin us on December 2nd\, 12-1pm PT to h
 ear from Dr. Eduardo Bunge\, Ph.D. about "Enhancing Parent-Led Interventio
 ns Through Artificial Intelligence." \n\nThis presentation will summarize 
 a growing body of research on ParenteAI and Pat\, a generative AI conversa
 tional agent designed to complement evidence-based Parent Management Train
 ing (PMT). Previous studies have examined treatment fidelity\, feasibility
 \, acceptability\, user engagement\, satisfaction\, and therapeutic allian
 ce. Preliminary findings indicate high adherence to PMT components\, subst
 antial caregiver engagement\, and high satisfaction. An initial pilot stud
 y found significant reductions in child behavioral problems and parental d
 epression\, anxiety\, and stress. Subsequent studies provided additional e
 vidence supporting the feasibility and acceptability of integrating Pat in
 to therapist-led group PMT. The presentation will also share findings from
  a preregistered randomized controlled trial (RCT) comparing therapist-led
  group PMT supplemented by Pat with the same intervention delivered withou
 t AI support.
END:VEVENT
