SUMMARY:[現場] Anastasia: The Musical
LOCATION:Dinkelspiel Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/anastasia-win27-1
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54541313334256.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/anas
 tasia-win27-1\n\nRussia\, 1927. Ten years after the Revolution toppled the
  Romanov family\, a rumor lingers among the people that the youngest royal
  daughter\, Anastasia\, survived. We follow a young woman named Anya\, who
  remembers almost nothing of her past\, as she joins a quick-thinking con 
 man and a former aristocrat on a journey to Paris to convince the Dowager 
 Empress that Anya is her long-lost granddaughter. With a Soviet officer on
  their trail and fragments of memory beginning to surface\, Anya must face
  a question she never expected: what if the story they have rehearsed is h
 er own?\n\nStanford’s vocalists and instrumentalists present Anastasia\,
  the 2016 musical inspired by the beloved 1997 animated film\, a story abo
 ut who we become when the past goes missing.\n\nDirected by Ariela Morgens
 tern\, with Musical Director Marie-Louise Catsalis and Vocal Director Benj
 amin Liupaogo.\n\nBook by Terrence McNally\nMusic by Stephen Flaherty\nLyr
 ics by Lynn Ahrens\n\nInspired by the Twentieth Century Fox Motion Picture
 s by special arrangement with Buena Vista Theatrical\nFrom the play by Mar
 celle Maurette as adapted by Guy Bolton \n\nAdmission Information\nTickets
  on sale soon!\n\nGeneral – $40 | Seniors (65+) and Non-Stanford Student
 s – $30 | Stanford Students – $20All sales will incur a $4 online/phon
 e per-ticket feeStanford students with valid ID receive free admission to 
 special previews on January 20 & 21 at 7:30 PM.Anastasia is funded by the 
 Drs. Ben and A. Jess Shenson Fund at Stanford University.\nAnastasia is 
END:VEVENT
