BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54541897611819@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261122T082710Z
DTSTART:20261130T200000Z
DTEND:20261130T210000Z
SUMMARY:[混合] Richard Socher | The Eureka Machine: Why AI Is the Key to 
 Unlocking a New Era of Scientific Discoveries
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building\, 119
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/richard-socher-the-eureka-machine-why
 -ai-is-the-key-to-unlocking-a-new-era-of-scientific-discoveries
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54541897611819.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/rich
 ard-socher-the-eureka-machine-why-ai-is-the-key-to-unlocking-a-new-era-of-
 scientific-discoveries\n報名/票券: https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu
 /event/richard-socher-del-seminar-series/\n\nThe next\, maybe final\, fron
 tier of AI research is automating the process of knowledge discovery. By p
 ointing AI first at itself and then at the R&D process of all scientific d
 omains\, we can far exceed where human-led research can take us. Richard S
 ocher argues the current pace of scientific discovery has slowed significa
 ntly over the past several decades as the fields of science fragment and t
 he number of researchers focused on any one continues to shrink.\n\nThe an
 swer to this generational challenge is to automate the scientific method i
 tself. He will lay out the architecture of a full-stack scientific superin
 telligence: a living map of human knowledge\, a unified model of physical 
 reality\, high-fidelity simulation\, autonomous laboratories\, and an agen
 t swarm that works the way a scientific community does. He will explain wh
 y recursive self-improvement is how you build it and why the first science
  to automate is the science of AI itself\, and share early results from Re
 cursive\, the new company he co-founded to build it.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54543452550446@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261118T211609Z
DTSTART:20261208T013000Z
DTEND:20261208T030000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] The Poetic and the Photographic: A Conversation between Ja
 son Francisco and Alexander Nemerov
LOCATION:McMurtry Building\, Oshman Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-poetic-and-the-photographic-a-con
 versation-between-jason-francisco-and-alexander-nemerov
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54543452550446.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/the-
 poetic-and-the-photographic-a-conversation-between-jason-francisco-and-ale
 xander-nemerov\n\nJoin photographer Jason Francisco and art historian Alex
 ander Nemerov as they discuss their new publication\, Autobiography of an 
 Unknown American\, a book of Francisco’s photographs\, made and found at
  various sites across the contemporary United States\, accompanied by Neme
 rov’s poems.\n\nThe book is a field guide to the lost corners of America
 \, a book of lamentation and praise\, a sustained encounter with the sorro
 w that American civilization shelters within itself—a dialogue of afterm
 aths and reckonings.  \n\nJason Francisco is an artist and essayist who jo
 ins documentary and conceptual art\, focusing on questions of historical m
 emory and witness. Francisco’s large-scale projects include the book Ali
 ve and Destroyed: A Meditation on the Holocaust in Time. He is a professor
  at Emory University.\n\nAlexander Nemerov is the author of many books on 
 American art and culture\, including Fierce Poise: Helen Frankenthaler and
  1950s America and The Forest: A Fable of America in the 1830s. He is the 
 Carl and Marilynn Thoma Provostial Professor in the Arts and Humanities at
  Stanford University.\n\nPhoto credit: Alex Ramos\n\nVISITOR INFORMATION\n
 Oshman Hall is located in the McMurtry Building on Stanford campus at 355 
 Roth Way. Visitor parking is free after 4pm on weekdays\, except by the Ov
 al. Alternatively\, take the Caltrain to Palo Alto Transit Center and ride
  the free Stanford Marguerite Shuttle. If you need a disability-related ac
 commodation or wheelchair access information\, please contact Julian
END:VEVENT
