SUMMARY:[線上] L.A.S.E.R.: A conversation about poet Fernando Pessoa
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/laser-a-conversation-about-poet-ferna
 ndo-pessoa-2339
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54567357981773.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/lase
 r-a-conversation-about-poet-fernando-pessoa-2339\n\nRegister here: https:/
 /stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_7lJ8n_2MSmmUPzyjngS5pg#/registration
  \n\nThe LASERs (Leonardo Art Science Evening Rendezvous) are an internati
 onal program of evening gatherings that bring artists and scientists toget
 her for informal presentations and conversation with an audience\, chaired
  by cultural historian Piero Scaruffi. This is the online segment of the D
 ecember LASER and will be devoted to a conversation about one of the great
 est writers of the 20th century:\n\n- Richard Zenith (Author) on "Fernando
  Pessoa: An Experimental Life" at 12pm California time (evening in Europe)
 .\n\nRichard Zenith is an acclaimed translator and literary critic\, best 
 known for his numerous English editions and studies of Fernando Pessoa’s
  work. In 2021 Zenith published the 1\,055-page biography "Pessoa: An Expe
 rimental Life"\, which was a finalist for the Pulitzer Prize.\n\nBesides P
 essoa\, some other outstanding translations include: the medieval antholog
 y "113 Galician-Portuguese Troubadour Poems" (1995)\; "Education by Stone:
  Selected Poems of João Cabral de Melo Neto"(Archipelago\, 2005)\, which 
 won the 2006 translation award from the Academy of American Poets\; "Multi
 tudinous Heart" (2015) a comprehensive collection of poems by Brazilian wr
 iter Carlos Drummond de Andrade.\n\nDetailed bio at: Leonardo Art Science 
 Evening Rendezvous LASER\n\nThe Stanford LASERs are co-sponsored by the de
 ans of Humanities and Sciences\, Engineering and Medicine\, and by Chemica
 l Engineering.
END:VEVENT
