SUMMARY:[現場]  The Long History of Amanuenses: Aides to Scholars and Aut
 hors from Antiquity to AI
LOCATION:East Asian Library\, 338
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-long-history-of-amanuenses-aides-
 to-scholars-and-authors-from-antiquity-to-ai-6807
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54570552552720.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/the-
 long-history-of-amanuenses-aides-to-scholars-and-authors-from-antiquity-to
 -ai-6807\n\nThe techniques for making texts have changed across multiple m
 edia and historical contexts since antiquity\, but a regular feature of th
 e work of authors and scholars through all those changes is the reliance o
 n helpers or amanuenses. Blair will discuss the factors that have made the
 m both invisible and occasionally visible\, the kind of work they did\, an
 d offer some examples of their trajectories in a few different periods. We
  can ponder together the extent to which AI fits into and deviates from ea
 rlier patterns of assistance.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
